    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Bildad’s Third Response to Job"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then Bildad the Shuhite replied:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“God is powerful and dreadful.",
          "He enforces peace in the heavens."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who is able to count his heavenly army?",
          "Doesn’t his light shine on all the earth?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "How can a mortal be innocent before God?",
          "Can anyone born of a woman be pure?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "God is more glorious than the moon;",
          "he shines brighter than the stars."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "In comparison, people are maggots;",
          "we mortals are mere worms.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
